<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X(\infty )$ be an arbitrary object of $\calX $. By Lemma <a href="/tag/75543A" data-tag="75543A">7.2.1.11</a> we can find a Postnikov tower 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X(\infty ) \rightarrow \ldots \rightarrow X(1) \rightarrow X(0). \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $X(n)$ is $n$-truncated, it belongs to $\calX ^{\wedge }$ by Corollary <a href="/tag/E03B1C" data-tag="E03B1C">6.5.1.14</a>. By Proposition <a href="/tag/3409BB" data-tag="3409BB">7.2.1.10</a>, the tower exhibits $X(\infty )$ as a limit of objects of $\calX ^{\wedge }$, so that $X(\infty )$ belongs to $\calX ^{\wedge }$ as well since the full subcategory $\calX ^{\wedge } \subseteq \calX $ is stable under limits. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>